{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150524-using-sam-haight","id":1150524,"title":"Using Sam Haight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-17T19:28:29-07:00","id":1150524,"title":"Using Sam Haight","content":"Alright, so....I'm deep diving old Werewolf books to build a new chronicle from and...I like the basic concept of Sam Haight.<br /> <br /> Can anyone give me some suggestions on using Haight without letting the ridiculous stuff he got into later leak in? Because at some point down the line, I'd like to put these same players through the Skinner SAS and I'd like the players to have some history with Haight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T20:43:06-07:00","id":1150536,"title":"","content":"Haight first appeared in the early supplement Valkenburg Foundation where one of the scenarios was him hunting Lunatics in the woods, specifically lupus Lunatics who couldn't change but were otherwise thinking sane. He killed them because they were easy prey - there were Garou for purposes of the ritual and had Rage and Gnosis, but were otherwise underpowered - no Gifts or Rites and couldn't assume other forms. His escape power was a Black Spiral Dancer fetish which allowed him to reform in the Umbra like a spirit in slumber (in some ares protected by the Wyrm).<br /> <br /> All the weird crossover stuff happened after that.<br /> <br /> If you want to use Haight, I suggest you run some kind of plot similar to that to begin with. That introduces him and his threat. Then after it's done, you can name drop him in whatever other plots you'd like to run. Since he is a kinfolk and has knowledge of the Garou, he'd be a good ally for many other bad guys as he could give them proper intelligence about their enemies (the PCs). That will keep the PCs after him and view him as an ongoing threat. Then you can run the Skinner to end that long story plot.<br /> <br /> Another option is prior to having him slay some Garou (who are for whatever reasons easy prey) is to include him as an element in the PCs or home sept backstory. So they are aware of the name, but only know him as a kinfolk ally or friend. They don't know he is harboring these dark thoughts. They only know he disappeared a while ago (to explain his adventures where he learns Wyrm lore and other things so he can return to perform the Rite of Sacred Rebirth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T01:37:50-07:00","id":1150576,"title":"","content":"I use him right now in my chronicle. In some way.<br /> <br /> 1. I don't like to use the meta plot in any way outside the ground structure of the setting I play. The players mostly don't know the meta plot so I can slightly use it by refering to it, without taking it as a whole storyline.<br /> 2. I despise this character.<br /> 3. I think the power level of the character makes it unuseable in any direct way.<br /> <br /> In my story he's only refered as H. Or better: I have an NPC that is refered as H.<br /> He sent an NPC - which is directly interacting with the PCs - to retrieve a diary H. used to document his research on the Rite of Sacred Rebirth.<br /> The book is in the hands of a mage - I couldn't really think of another creature, that could realisticly kill five garou - who want's to use it to perform the rite.<br /> <br /> That's it. I will never refer to him by full name or let him appear in the chronicle.<br /> He's just... just too cringeworthy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T04:31:59-07:00","id":1150601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Novagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150524-using-sam-haight#post1150524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone give me some suggestions on using Haight without letting the ridiculous stuff he got into later leak in? Because at some point down the line, I'd like to put these same players through the Skinner SAS and I'd like the players to have some history with Haight</div> </div> </div> </div>Haight was born as a joke, and that's the reason his background is awful and nonsensical. Best thing is that a lot of people thought they were serious...<br /> Lore-wise (and I mean RAW, it's not an interpretation) neither vampires nor werewolves can use Awakened magick. So, if you want to use him as a ghouled kinfolk who learnt Thaumaturgy, sure - but I'd lower his 6th gen Tremere master to something more sensible and cap down his knowledge of it. The skin-dancing is also fine, but that's just as far as I'd go: no Awakened magic, no adventures in the Underworld, and rework part of all that nonsense in the SAS Skinner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T08:30:02-07:00","id":1150647,"title":"","content":"What about Numina? Think it makes sense for a skin Dancer to have learned some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T09:37:07-07:00","id":1150670,"title":"","content":"I've wanted to use him in an overblown way. Recurring villain, skin walking, hedge magic casting with more than one garou and fera skin to use. I name dropped him once in a game but the game ended before that plot was engaged. The PCs had other things on their minds at the time.<br /> <br /> If I did run a game, the PCs will know about him but even more overblown. Muahah It partly comes down to misreading him the first time so I made up some hedge magic that has bound his soul to each of the skins. The plan was: the PCs had to find his lair and destroy the skins to get rid of him. He wouldn't have been overly powerful as an individual but had plenty of back up plans and so forth. I thought it would be a neat story. Unless they focused on him, he would hit and run. Showing up every few sessions to harass, but not a major threat. It's how I intended to use him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:23:48-07:00","id":1150728,"title":"","content":"Height is - or at least was as originally conceived - a sort of boogieman/morality tale for the Garou. &quot;Be nice to your Kin, or they could turn into the Skinner.&quot; If used well, he becomes a window into Garou/Kinfolk relations, issues of emotional abuse and ostracization (something that should resonate with almost all Metis as well as a lot of Homids), and the idea of the hunters becoming the hunted. The main reason he's so dangerous is because he knows all of the Garou's weaknesses and is such a skilled hunter that knows how to stalk, trap and kill them. All the shapeshifting and wizardry from later is just window dressing. At the core is this uber-predator who deep down inside just wants to dominate and earn the fear of the people who abused, degraded and bullied him as a child and young man. Specifically, his father, who died in a freak accident when Height was a teenager, thus robbing him of any sort of closure. Essentially a serial killer whose target of choice happens to be werewolves. (He's basically Buffalo Bill from Silence of the Lambs, with magic that will make his &quot;woman suit&quot; really turn him into a woman; Most of the psychological insights Dr. Lector gives about Bill applied to Height as well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T13:33:15-07:00","id":1150757,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind also that while Haight is gone, the Skin Dancers are not. If you don't want the overpowered aspects of Haight in the chronicle, you can just as easily make the antagonist some random Kin who starts to drift down the Skin Dancer path. That was always really the scary part of what Haight represented; The Garou were dependent upon their Kin for all sorts of stuff, but there was always a gulf between them -- and the inherent risk that people who knew so much about them (and their strengths and weaknesses) would turn on them as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T20:04:50-07:00","id":1150877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150524-using-sam-haight?p=1150647#post1150647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Numina? Think it makes sense for a skin Dancer to have learned some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Numina are fine, but manuals say that's extremely rare for people to have just one. So, since the point is to remove the nonsense from Haight, I wouldn't give him more than one - and only picking from the occult-shamanic list, surely not a psychic themed numen. The Conjuration numen would fit well, just to say one, and replace Thaumaturgy as occult knowledge (he may still know the theory behind disciplines from when he was a ghoul, but since he can't keep vampire blood in him anymore he won't be able to use them).<br /> <br /> By the way, is there any source for Numina in the 20th editions beside K:aBA? Don't think they remade Sorcerer yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T06:41:59-07:00","id":1152783,"title":"","content":"If you want Height to be able to do (black) magic, the easiest way is to give him the ability to do any Rites (especially Black Spiral Dancer/Wyrm ones) the Storyteller deems necessary for the story, and if you have access to some of the Vampire stuff, to covert some of the various Blood Magic rituals into Rites as well. At least that's what I've always done for human sorcerers/witches/wizards when running Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T08:38:22-07:00","id":1152815,"title":"","content":"I think what I'm going to do is use the initial Haight story from Valkenburg Foundation, let him escape (Unless my players manage to do something truly extraordinary), bring him back later on with a custom built story, kill him off there, then star laying the seeds for the Skinner SAS over the course of the next several story arcs. <br /> <br /> And I think I'm just going to ignore all the ghouling, sphere magic and such. (Unless someone has an idea to use that stuff that keeps it from becoming ridiculous)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T09:40:08-07:00","id":1152832,"title":"","content":"You could always make him an angry ashtray (that he was soul forged into). Kidding, kidding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T17:45:43-07:00","id":1152987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150524-using-sam-haight?p=1152832#post1152832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always make him an angry ashtray (that he was soul forged into). Kidding, kidding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angry Ashtrays: the WoD equivalent of Angry Birds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T22:11:34-07:00","id":1153675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Novagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150524-using-sam-haight?p=1152815#post1152815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I think I'm just going to ignore all the ghouling, sphere magic and such. (Unless someone has an idea to use that stuff that keeps it from becoming ridiculous)</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you are running some sort of crazy crossover plot where you need them, this is the best bet. Its a werewolf game I'd just give him an assortment of gifts and Rites taken from through out the setting with some implication that he could steal pretty freely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T07:39:24-08:00","id":1166464,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it I would run Sam as a Garou serial killer somewhere between Jason and Jigsaw. Travelling around the world righting the wrong in his head or those of disaffected Kinfolk. Having a skinned werewolf found in your territory tells you the &quot;Skinner&quot; has arrived. He,d be armed the teeth with not only modern weapons but also stolen fetishes. The pack may think.to aim him at the nearest Pit but that would only make him stronger and likely the banes that follow in his wake will grow in power too. That said I wouldn't run him as an agent of he Wyrm. The rest of the cross over stuff you can easily ignore, his greatest contribution beyond some insane modules was the Skin Walkers so he still has a place in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":982,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","user":"Cptmachine","date":". 12-10-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T11:16:00-08:00","id":1166502,"title":"","content":"Sam got a lot of weird stuff because he was the first cross-over villain. He needed equivalent powers on other splats he prayed upon, and it was done the way it was.<br /> <br /> In the end, you have half a dozen aspects of the character that you can take or let down. He is the kin that prey upon Garou, the Ghoul that prey upon Vampires, the Sorcerer that preys upon Mage for power. He is the Hedge Magician that stole the power of the splat to use against its supposed masters. He is the defender of kinfolk and forefather of the Skin Dancers. And he is a psychopathic serial killer.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to &quot;fix&quot; Height is to keep only the aspects you need, and the relevant powers, and then translate whatever is left only to the mechanics of your actual game. Thaumaturgy and the bogus Staff of True Magick(tm), specially, are just ways of making his knowledge of Rites work in other splats. It isn't the same mechanic, but it is the same narrative function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}